.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt CMS_ADD0_CERT 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm CMS_add0_cert ,
.Nm CMS_add1_cert ,
.Nm CMS_get1_certs ,
.Nm CMS_add0_crl ,
.Nm CMS_add1_crl ,
.Nm CMS_get1_crls
.Nd CMS certificate and CRL utility functions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/cms.h
.Ft int
.Fo CMS_add0_cert
.Fa "CMS_ContentInfo *cms"
.Fa "X509 *cert"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo CMS_add1_cert
.Fa "CMS_ContentInfo *cms"
.Fa "X509 *cert"
.Fc
.Bd -literal
 STACK_OF(X509) *CMS_get1_certs(CMS_ContentInfo *cms);
.Ed
.Ft int
.Fo CMS_add0_crl
.Fa "CMS_ContentInfo *cms"
.Fa "X509_CRL *crl"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo CMS_add1_crl
.Fa "CMS_ContentInfo *cms"
.Fa "X509_CRL *crl"
.Fc
.Bd -literal
 STACK_OF(X509_CRL) *CMS_get1_crls(CMS_ContentInfo *cms);
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn CMS_add0_cert
and
.Fn CMS_add1_cert
add certificate
.Fa cert
to
.Fa cms
unless it is already present.
This is used by
.Xr CMS_sign_ex 3
and
.Xr CMS_sign 3
and may be used before calling
.Xr CMS_verify 3
to help chain building in certificate validation.
As the 0 implies,
.Fn CMS_add0_cert
adds
.Fa cert
internally to
.Fa cms
and on success it must not be freed up by the caller.
In contrast, the caller of
.Fn CMS_add1_cert
must free
.Fa cert .
.Fa cms
must be of type signed data or (authenticated) enveloped data.
For signed data, such a certificate can be used when signing or
verifying to fill in the signer certificate or to provide an extra CA
certificate that may be needed for chain building in certificate
validation.
.Pp
.Xr CMS_get1_certs 3
returns all certificates in
.Fa cms .
.Pp
.Fn CMS_add0_crl
and
.Fn CMS_add1_crl
add CRL
.Fa crl
to
.Fa cms .
.Fa cms
must be of type signed data or (authenticated) enveloped data.
For signed data, such a CRL may be used in certificate validation with
.Xr CMS_verify 3 .
It may be given both for inclusion when signing a CMS message and when
verifying a signed CMS message.
.Pp
.Xr CMS_get1_crls 3
returns all CRLs in
.Fa cms .
.Sh NOTES
The CMS_ContentInfo structure
.Fa cms
must be of type signed data or enveloped data or authenticated enveloped
data or an error will be returned.
.Pp
For signed data, certificates and CRLs are added to the
.Em certificates
and
.Em crls
fields of SignedData structure.
For enveloped data they are added to
.Sy OriginatorInfo .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn CMS_add0_cert ,
.Fn CMS_add1_cert
and
.Fn CMS_add0_crl
and
.Fn CMS_add1_crl
return 1 for success and 0 for failure.
.Pp
.Xr CMS_get1_certs 3
and
.Xr CMS_get1_crls 3
return the STACK of certificates or CRLs or NULL if there are none or an
error occurs.
Besides out-of-memory, the only error which will occur in practice is if
the
.Fa cms
type is invalid.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr CMS_sign 3 ,
.Xr CMS_sign_ex 3 ,
.Xr CMS_verify 3 ,
.Xr CMS_encrypt 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn CMS_add0_cert
and
.Fn CMS_add1_cert
have been changed in OpenSSL 3.2 not to throw an error if a certificate
to be added is already present.
